   144	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   145	    """
   146	    Slide every grey diagonal segment along its yellow polarity tip and recolor it by the edge-bar segment it lands against.
   147	
   148	    Input structure:
   149	    - The outermost row and column form 1-cell-wide colored edge bars, each split into multiple visible color segments.
   150	    - The interior is black except for several diagonal 4-pixel launchers made of three grey cells plus one yellow tip cell on one endpoint.
   151	    - Each launcher is an 8-connected straight diagonal chain, and the yellow tip indicates which diagonal direction it travels.
   152	
   153	    Rule:
   154	    - For each launcher, move the whole 4-pixel object one diagonal step at a time in the yellow tip's direction.
   155	    - Stop when the yellow tip first enters an interior cell that is directly adjacent to exactly one edge bar.
   156	    - Clear the launcher's original position, then repaint all four of its landed cells with the color of the contacted edge-bar segment.
   157	    - Keep all edge bars unchanged.
   158	
   159	    Key insight:
   160	    - The yellow endpoint is a polarity marker, not decoration: it fixes the travel direction, while the final color is determined only by the exact border segment touched at the tip's landing position.
